{"name":"Luigi","hex":"#4cbb17","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Luigi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male given name from Italian, equivalent to English Louis."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To assassinate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Luigi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Luigi (given name)","blocks":[{"text":"Luigi is a masculine Italian given name. It is the Italian form of the German name Ludwig, through the Latinization Ludovicus, corresponding to the French name Louis and its anglicized variant Lewis."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luigi_(given_name)","wikidata":"Q4245067"},{"title":"Luigi (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Luigi is a character created by Japanese video game designer Shigeru Miyamoto. Part of Nintendo's Mario franchise, he is a kind-hearted, cowardly Italian plumber, and Mario's slightly younger twin brother and partner of Mario. Like his brother, Luigi's distinctive characteristics include his large nose and mustache, overalls, hat, and medium-pitched, exaggerated Italian accent."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/be/Luigi_by_Shigehisa_Nakaue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luigi_(character)","wikidata":"Q210593"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Charles_Martinet_Photo_Op_GalaxyCon_Richmond_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Charles_Martinet_Photo_Op_GalaxyCon_Richmond_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Charles_Martinet_Photo_Op_GalaxyCon_Richmond_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Charles_Martinet_Photo_Op_GalaxyCon_Richmond_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Martinet_Photo_Op_GalaxyCon_R